WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.910
It is the full moon.

2
00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.490
Inside a boundary marked by
stones, a group of monks gathers.

3
00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.520
No lay people are present.

4
00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:12.790
First, the monks sit in pairs
and confess any offences.

5
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:18.440
Then one monk recites all
227 rules, from memory.

6
00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:22.070
Why confess first, before
the rules are even heard?

7
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.800
In this mission, you'll
see how the rules grew,

8
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.730
case by case, and how they
are graded by seriousness.

9
00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:32.000
Then you'll meet the four
gravest offences of all,

10
00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.130
the most serious rules in the whole code.

11
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:40.190
Your mission: explain why Theravada monks
confess to each other before the rules

12
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.170
are recited.
